@startuml sd_event_to_read_model
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontSize 16
title Scenario: a command, its event and the read models (CQRS, transactional outbox)

autonumber
actor "ATCC" as c
participant "aircraft-maintenance-1" as am1
database "its H2\n(aircraft, event_outbox)" as db1
participant "EventRelay\n(aircraft-maintenance-1)" as relay
queue "RabbitMQ\naircraft-maintenance.events" as ex
participant "aircraft-maintenance-0..2\n(read-model queues)" as amr
participant "airports-routes-0..2\nflight-ops-0..2" as others

c -> am1 : POST /api/aircrafts (command)
group one transaction
  am1 -> db1 : insert aircraft (write model)
  am1 -> db1 : replica_state stamp (time, replica)
  am1 -> db1 : insert event_outbox (aircraft.created, stamp, data)
end
am1 --> c : 201 (does not wait for the broker)
am1 -> relay : after the commit: relay soon
relay -> ex : publish aircraft.created (persistent)
ex --> relay : confirm
relay -> db1 : delete the outbox entry
note right of relay
  Broker down: the entry stays,
  retried every 0.5 s, in order
end note
ex -> amr : one quorum queue per replica
amr -> amr : apply if later than the row (last writer wins)
ex -> others : their queues, bound to aircraft.*
others -> others : their copy of the fleet

note over amr, others
  Queries read these local copies: GET /api/aircrafts, /api/v2/unicorns,
  compatible routes, scheduling. A message that cannot be applied goes to the
  dead-letter queue after 5 attempts; snapshots and reconciliation repair the row.
end note
@enduml
